<p>Corpus Christi storm damage claims cover a wide range of weather. In a single year, the Coastal Bend can see spring hail, squall lines with damaging straight-line winds, brief tornadoes, tropical storms, flash flooding, and the occasional hard freeze. NOAA's Storm Events Database lists 973 weather reports for Nueces County since 1953, including 287 thunderstorm wind reports, 134 hail reports, 107 tornado reports, and 256 flash flood reports. If you own a home or business in Corpus Christi, Nueces County, or nearby communities, this page explains how storm claims generally work and how a public adjuster may help.</p>
<p>Many storm claims involve more than one type of damage, and sometimes more than one insurance policy. Sorting that out early helps keep the claim on track. Our <a href="/corpus-christi-storm-history-hail-wind-hurricanes/">Corpus Christi storm history article</a> has more local background.</p>

